# Ebb currently has no required environment variables.
#
# The app makes no network requests and has no backend — every feature
# (journal, memories, breathing, the local "AI companion") runs entirely
# on-device against data stored in AsyncStorage/SecureStore. There is
# nothing to configure here for a production build to work.
#
# This file exists as a placeholder and a convention: if you add a real
# network feature later (analytics, a sync backend, a hosted AI model),
# put its config here as EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables (client-exposed) or a
# plain name (server/build-time only — e.g. read by app.config.js), copy
# this file to `.env` with real values, and never commit `.env` itself.
#
# Example shape for when that day comes:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOME_SERVICE_URL=https://example.com
